  "result": "The gate now returns **OK** for NRS_484B_113_2 (9 witnesses), after 3 of the 6 allowed runs.\n\n**Rule** (`NRS_484B_113_2.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a member of the vehicle group defined in DEF-NRS-484A-320.\n- **When it applies:** any one of three cases:\n  1. **Into an intersection:** the car's footprint starts to overlap an intersection at this moment.\n  2. **On a crosswalk:** the car's footprint overlaps a crosswalk.\n  3. **Around a street corner:** the place is inside city limits, the car is turning, and its footprint is on an intersection.\n- **What it forbids:** backing.\n\nThis follows the blueprint as written. I added no readings of my own.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **Untouched skeleton:** all six names the node uses were reported unused.\n2. **After writing the rule and scenes:** `WITNESS_FAIL` on branch_2, branch_3 and branch_5. In those scenes the car had a turning rate but its heading never changed, which real data can't produce.\n3. **After the fix:** `OK`. The fix was to turn 90°/s over each 1 s step, so the heading moves a quarter turn per step and the direction values stay exact.\n\n**Changes to the witnesses:**\n- **Time window:** every scenario is judged only at 1000–2000 ms. \"Starts to overlap the intersection\" compares with the previous moment, so it can't be decided at the first one.\n- **branch_4 (new, not applicable):** the car backs straight inside an intersection it had already entered. This tests the turning condition, and shows that entering differs from just being inside.\n- **branch_5 (new, not applicable):** the car backs while turning in mid-block, with no intersection under it.\n\n**Wasted calls:** before the first real run I tried two other gate commands (`--help` and `--dry`). The permission system blocked both and neither ran.\n\nThe run log and reasoning are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
